  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef ml_softmax_regression(X: list, y: list, num_classes: int = 3, lr: float = 0.1, epochs: int = 10) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Softmax Regression** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef ml_softmax_regression(X: list, y: list, num_classes: int = 3, lr: float = 0.1, epochs: int = 10) -> dict:\n    Xa, ya, K = np.array(X, dtype=np.float64), np.array(y, dtype=np.int64), int(num_classes)\n    N, D = Xa.shape; W = np.zeros((D, K))\n    Y = np.zeros((N, K)); Y[np.arange(N), ya] = 1.0\n    for _ in range(int(epochs)):\n        l = np.dot(Xa, W); ex = np.exp(l - np.max(l, axis=1, keepdims=True))\n        p = ex / np.sum(ex, axis=1, keepdims=True)\n        W -= float(lr) * (np.dot(Xa.T, p - Y) / N)\n    p_final = np.argmax(np.dot(Xa, W), axis=1)\n    return {'weights': np.round(W, 4).tolist(), 'train_accuracy': round(float(np.mean(p_final == ya)), 4)}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
